WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.790
Speaker 1: This one is just an absolute beauty
that in a sense doesn't surprise me.

00:00:05.790 --> 00:00:09.150
But it seems like it would be satire if you
didn't know any better.

00:00:09.150 --> 00:00:15.130
During a recent segment on Fox News, a Fox
News anchor asked Republican Senator Mike

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:22.490
Braun from Indiana whether Joe Biden's economy
is essentially too good for Joe Biden to be

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:25.039
doing the things that he wants to do.

00:00:25.039 --> 00:00:29.640
This is hilarious for several reasons which
we will get to now.

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:35.271
As many of you know, the stock market, which
Donald Trump told us would crash if Joe Biden

00:00:35.271 --> 00:00:39.030
became president, has actually hit record
highs.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:44.090
New unemployment claims are the lowest they've
been since the start of the pandemic, and

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.519
they're going lower every single week.

00:00:46.519 --> 00:00:49.859
Joe Biden's vaccination plan is really popular.

00:00:49.859 --> 00:00:54.660
Joe Biden's coronavirus stimulus package,
which passed in March, is very popular.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:00.300
Joe Biden's proposed infrastructure package
is quite popular and things are just recovering

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:04.010
and sort of boring and increasingly looking
good.

00:01:04.010 --> 00:01:06.990
It doesn't mean we've solved every problem
or even nearly that.

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:11.610
But in terms of comparing to what was going
on under Trump, things are looking pretty

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:12.610
good.

00:01:12.610 --> 00:01:18.430
So here is a Fox News host saying the stock
market's doing great.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.430
Unemployment is down.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:21.500
Why is Joe Biden doing things?

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:26.060
Isn't it dangerous to be doing things when
the economy is booming?

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.630
It's almost like things are too good.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:29.630
Take a look at this passing.

00:01:29.630 --> 00:01:35.399
Speaker 2: Seeing a booming American economy,
whether it's the jobs market, the Dow, as

00:01:35.399 --> 00:01:38.260
you see on your screen there, continues to
hit record highs.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.229
You've got wages moving higher.

00:01:40.229 --> 00:01:47.020
So why is it that this administration wants
to spend all this money when it seems things

00:01:47.020 --> 00:01:48.020
are getting better?

00:01:48.020 --> 00:01:56.009
Speaker 3: Well, that's a good question, because
the real consequences will be felt probably

00:01:56.009 --> 00:01:57.579
post 2022.

00:01:57.579 --> 00:02:03.130
And they're calculating all this expertly
in my mind, politically.

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:06.210
Speaker 1: Isn't that just something else?

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:11.099
All of this time, they've been denying that
things are actually going well.

00:02:11.099 --> 00:02:17.510
And now all of a sudden with concern, they
say, oh, I don't know, the economy's booming,

00:02:17.510 --> 00:02:21.130
the stock market's booming, the job market
is recovering.

00:02:21.130 --> 00:02:23.200
And yet Joe Biden wants to do all this stuff.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:24.200
I don't know.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:28.980
That sounds like it could be dangerous to
do things when the economy is doing so well.

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:31.140
And Mike Braun, of course, throwing in.

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:35.720
Well, you know, the stuff Joe Biden wants
to do won't be good in the long term.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:39.600
It might get him to twenty, twenty two in
good shape, but it's not going to be good

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.200
in the long term, which is a consideration
that they never make when they are pulling

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:47.640
their hair brained economic policy.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:53.550
When a Republican is in power, they are so
desperate that it's actually hilarious.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:59.129
Oh, no, the economy is booming and yet Joe
Biden still is doing things.

00:02:59.129 --> 00:03:01.159
It's beyond parody.

00:03:01.159 --> 00:03:06.940
They're essentially admitting that Biden is
so good at running the country, he shouldn't

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:09.269
even really be doing anything else.

00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:12.750
And the fact that he's trying to should really
concern all of us.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:19.390
The economy's doing dangerously well under
Joe Biden, and that could be a disaster.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:24.910
Now, there's also a serious thing here, which
is, of course, a lot of the jobs that are

00:03:24.910 --> 00:03:28.810
coming back for now are coming back part time.

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.409
They were full time, many of these jobs.

00:03:30.409 --> 00:03:31.409
Why?

00:03:31.409 --> 00:03:33.319
Well, we're in the middle of a pandemic recovery.

00:03:33.319 --> 00:03:38.189
And as industries start to open, as different
sectors start to open, some of these jobs

00:03:38.189 --> 00:03:41.129
will come back not provisionally, but on a
part time basis.

00:03:41.129 --> 00:03:43.890
Many businesses operating with reduced hours.

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:47.980
The recovery has been disproportionately better.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.700
For the very rich than it has for everybody
else, it's been the pandemic has been really

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:57.420
good for the ultra super rich and it has been
that kind of case shaped recovery that we've

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:58.989
talked about before.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:05.310
Much of the stock market performance, which
has been stellar, goes to the very rich.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:11.840
So there is a real question, which is even
though the economy is doing quite well for

00:04:11.840 --> 00:04:14.790
wealthy people, what about everybody else?

00:04:14.790 --> 00:04:18.970
And that's exactly what Joe Biden's spending
programs are trying to work on.

00:04:18.970 --> 00:04:25.390
But we are at a point where even doing well
now is considered bad.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:30.290
If you then continue trying to do more things,
as Joe Biden is trying to do, they have nothing

00:04:30.290 --> 00:04:31.290
else to whine about.

00:04:31.290 --> 00:04:38.420
We've gotten to the is the economy too good
part of the Joe Biden presidency?

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:43.521
And it's only like on month four, they were
just trying to give Trump credit for the economy

00:04:43.521 --> 00:04:45.080
last week.

00:04:45.080 --> 00:04:50.050
Now it's well, this is Biden's economy, but
it's almost like it's doing so well.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:54.330
Something must be about to go wrong or it
must be terrible for Joe Biden to keep trying

00:04:54.330 --> 00:04:55.800
to do stuff.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:01.380
If you were to write a Saturday Night Live
script about how Fox News would cover the

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:06.351
circumstances now four months in three or
four months into Joe Biden's presidency, it

00:05:06.351 --> 00:05:10.640
would be indistinguishable from is the economy
doing dangerously well?

00:05:10.640 --> 00:05:13.010
And that's exactly what we're getting on FOX
News.

